[' Here's a high-level architecture design for the requested Java application:

1. **Data Ingestion Layer:**
   - Microservices responsible for ingesting data from geographically dispersed sources. Each microservice will use appropriate APIs to handle intermittent network connectivity and partial service availability.
   - Kafka streams for real-time data processing and fault tolerance.

2. **Union-Find Data Structure:**
   - Implement Union-Find data structure in Java, optimized for performance under peak loads.
   - Calculate the number of disjoint pairs of elements in an integer array using the Union-Find data structure:

```java
import java.util.*;
public class UF {
    private int[] id;  // id[i] = parent of i
    private int count; // number of sets

    public UF(int size) {
        id = new int[size];
        for (int i = 0; i < size; ++i) id[i] = i;
        count = size;
    }

    // find the set of p and q are in
    public int find(int p) {
        validate(p);
        stack<Integer> path = new Stack<>();
        while (p != id[p]) {
            path.push(p);
            p = id[p];
        }
        while (!path.isEmpty()) {
            int q = path.pop();
            id[q] = p;
        }
        return p;
    }

    // merge the sets of p and q, making them the same set
    public void union(int p, int q) {
        int rootP = find(p);
        int rootQ = find(q);
        id[rootP] = rootQ;
        count--;
    }

    private void validate(int p) {
        if (p < 0 || p >= id.length)
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("index " + p + " is out of bounds");
    }

    public int count() { return count; }
}
```

